      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Published alignment: CG/CN.</p><h2>Description</h2><p>This dragon's scales are the color of ocean's waves, this hatchling, serpentine dragon moves with the waves themselves. Blue dragons are usually found by large bodies of water.</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 12, touch 11, flat-footed 12 (-1 dex, +1 natural, +2 size)</p><p>hp 25 (3d12)</p><p>Fort +5, Ref +2, Will +4</p><p>Immune Water, Paralysis, Sleep; Resist Fire 50%</p><p>Weakness Lightning</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 60 ft., swim 90 ft.</p><p>Melee Bite +4 (1d4-1), 2 Claws +4 (1d3-1)</p><p>Space 2.5 ft.; Reach 0 ft. (5 ft. with bite)</p><p>Special Attacks Breath Weapon (30-ft. line, 1d10 water damage, Reflex DC 11 half, usable every 1d4 rounds), Water Gun</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 9, Dex 8, Con 11, Int 8, Wis 13, Cha 10</p><p>Base Atk +3; CMB +4; CMD 13 (17 vs. trip)</p><p>Feats Great Fortitude, Improved Initiative</p><p>Skills Diplomacy +6, Perception +7, Stealth +9, Survival +7, Swim +13; Racial Modifiers +8 Swim</p><p>Languages Draconic</p><p>SQ water breathing</p>"
      }
